001"/></fig><fig id="fig2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>The FungalWeb infrastructure.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJTA2009-917826.002"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>LIMS use case diagram.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJTA2009-917826.003"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Illustration of the MYCO-LIMS FR traceability model.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJTA2009-917826.004"/></fig><fig id="fig5" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Illustration of the MYCO-LIMS NFR traceability model.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJTA2009-917826.005"/></fig><fig id="fig6" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Illustrationof MYCO-LIMS NFRs/FRs dependencies hierarchical model.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJTA2009-917826.006"/></fig><fig id="fig7" position="float"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>MYCO-LIMS requirements associations' refinement.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJTA2009-917826.007"/></fig><fig id="fig8" position="float"><label>Figure 8</label><caption><p>Generic categorical framework for requirement traceability.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJTA2009-917826.008"/></fig><fig id="fig9" position="float"><label>Figure 9</label><caption><p>					<italic>FR, NFR hierarchies, and relations</italic> category.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJTA2009-917826.009"/></fig><fig id="fig10" position="float"><label>Figure 10</label><caption><p>Tracing the changes to the state spaces, classes, and methods.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJTA2009-917826.010"/></fig><fig id="fig11" position="float"><label>Figure 11</label><caption><p>The RLR framework for change management and conflict resolution.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJTA2009-917826.011"/></fig><fig id="fig12" position="float"><label>Figure 12</label><caption><p>Two categorical constructors: (a) pushout, (b) pullback.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="IJT